k, and White has only one legal reply.","The next best move, 59…Rf5, would drop Black's winning chances from 95% to 50% (0.00).","59…Ra3+ wins the queen for a bishop, picking it up with 61…Rxb8.","Sets up a sequence and wins the queen for a bishop once the captures settle, picking it up with 61…Rxb8.","White answers 60.Kb5, attacking the bishop on c5, which is undefended."]},{"ply":120,"name":"60…Rb3+","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"60…Rb3+! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Skewers the king: when it moves, the queen on b8 behind it falls.","The rook takes the open b-file.","The next best move, 60…Bf2, would drop Black's winning chances from 96% to 45% (+0.53).","60…Rb3+ wins the queen for a bishop, picking it up with 61…Rxb8.","Sets up a sequence and wins the queen for a bishop once the captures settle, picking it up with 61…Rxb8.","White answers 61.Kxc5, taking the bishop on c5 and uncovering an attack on the rook on b3."]}],"opening":{"name":"Sicilian Defense: Old Sicilian","eco":"B30","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 5.O-O: 9 moves in all, 5 by White and 4 by Black.","Black left the book with 5…Qb6. In 249 games from this position, strong players played 5…a6 (82%), 5…Nd4 (7%), 5…Ng6 (4%) or 5…g6 (4%).","The main line goes on 5…a6 6.Bxc6 Nxc6 7.d4 cxd4 8.Nxd4 Qc7 9.Re1 Bd6.","From here White scored 55% in those games, with 13% drawn."]}}